traces/adsb-2026-11-05.jsonl.gz contains information from adsb.lol
(https://adsb.lol), made available under the Open Database License (ODbL)
v1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

It was recorded on 2026-11-05 from 18:17:41 to 19:17:41 UTC with

    gentrace -sensor a=39.0,-77.0,60 -sensor b=39.0,-76.2,60 -sensor c=39.0,-77.8,60 \
        -every 9s -duration 1h -out traces/adsb-2026-11-05.jsonl.gz

by polling the adsb.lol API for a 70 nm circle around 39.0,-77.0 once every
3 s and handing each response to the next sensor in turn. That was about twice
what the feed answers (10 requests a minute), so the recording is bursty:
nearly every minute, about 27 s of answers, then about 33 s of waiting out a
refusal. 601 of its 669 requests were answered and 68 failed; a sensor heard
its circle every 9 s at the median but every 18 s on average. Each line is a
position report as one sensor received it: t_ms is when, relative to the start
of the recording, and delay_ms how long after the observation.

The raw polls committed in results/live/raw and results/aws/raw, and the
recorded-hour-raw release asset, hold aircraft addresses and times taken from
adsb.lol too, so they are under the ODbL as well. If you redistribute any of
them, or a database derived from them, keep it under the ODbL. Everything else
in this repository is under the MIT license in LICENSE; seed1.jsonl is
synthetic and covered by it.
